{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "GEOSFP",
    "description": "GEOS-FP regridding model — the coupler half of the geosfp loader+regridding-model split (RFC pure-io-data-loaders §6/§7; bead esm-3nc.2, following the esm-3nc.1 era5/wrf pattern). Exposes NASA GMAO GEOS-FP assimilated meteorology (0.25°×0.3125° global, GEOS-Chem 72-level) on the simulation's target grid for coupling into EarthSciML systems.\n\nStructure (RFC §6): at 0.7.0 it declared the six pure-I/O GEOS-FP grid loaders as subsystems under their original names (GEOSFP_A1/A3cld/A3dyn/A3mstC/A3mstE/I3 → ./geosfp_<coll>_loader.esm); at esm 1.0.0 those six files are merged BACK into this one as the `data_sources` entries GEOSFP_A1 … GEOSFP_I3, keeping the SAME registry names, so fields are still referenced as GEOSFP.<coll>.<var> and re-exposed as model observeds (GEOSFP.T, GEOSFP.U, …). Each merged file's own metadata is preserved verbatim under its registry entry's metadata.merged_file_metadata. Native grids are geographic (longlat/WGS84) → longlat identity reprojection (esd-47z.1). Regridding is per-variable (`regrid`): A3dyn staggered winds U/V/OMEGA → B-spline (esd-47z.3); all other fields → conservative. The hybrid sigma-pressure Ap/Bp tables (former GEOSFP_hybrid_coefs kind:lookup, removed in the 0.6.0 hard break) are now the top-level function_tables geosfp_Ap_pa and geosfp_Bp, consumed by P = Ap(lev)+Bp(lev)·PS.\n\nDerived observeds on the target grid: pressure P, virtual temperature Tv and Tv_sfc, the level derivative δPδlev, and the lat/lon coordinate metrics δxδlon, δyδlat. MeanWind coupling: GEOSFP.U/V/OMEGA → MeanWind v_lon/v_lat/v_lev.\n\nMigrated from EarthSciData.jl@830435a065f27e99f10bba91107ca1730322cc6b:src/geosfp.jl:410 (GEOSFP constructor, esm-1c6s); split into pure loaders + regridding model by esm-3nc.2.",
    "tags": [
      "earthsci_data",
      "meteorology",
      "atmospheric_dynamics",
      "data_loader",
      "geos_fp",
      "global",
      "hybrid_pressure",
      "geos_chem",
      "nasa",
      "regridding_model",
      "longlat",
      "pure-io-split"
    ],
    "created": "2026-05-30T00:00:00Z",
    "authors": [
      "NASA GMAO / GEOS-Chem",
      "EarthSciModels migration (esm-3nc.2)"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "GEOS-FP data archived for GEOS-Chem classic. NASA Global Modeling and Assimilation Office (GMAO). AWS S3 mirror: s3://geos-chem/GEOS_{domain}/GEOS_FP/. See http://geoschemdata.wustl.edu/ExtData/ for current domain and file-type options.",
        "url": "http://geoschemdata.wustl.edu/ExtData/"
      },
      {
        "citation": "Molod, A., Takacs, L., Suarez, M., and Bacmeister, J. (2015). Development of the GEOS-5 atmospheric general circulation model: evolution from MERRA to MERRA2. Geosci. Model Dev., 8, 1339–1356.",
        "doi": "10.5194/gmd-8-1339-2015"
      },
      {
        "citation": "GEOS-Chem vertical grid documentation: https://wiki.seas.harvard.edu/geos-chem/index.php/GEOS-Chem_vertical_grids",
        "url": "https://wiki.seas.harvard.edu/geos-chem/index.php/GEOS-Chem_vertical_grids"
      },
      {
        "citation": "Source: EarthSciData.jl@830435a065f27e99f10bba91107ca1730322cc6b:src/geosfp.jl (GEOSFPFileSet, GEOSFP constructor, Ap/Bp hybrid grid coefficients, geosfp_staggering). Test: test/geosfp_test.jl. Docs: docs present in pinned commit."
      }
    ]
  },
