            72
          ]
        },
        "regridding_provenance": "Former co-located data_loaders.regridding block (fill_value=0.0, extrapolation=clamp) removed in the 0.6.0 hard break; regridding is now declared per-variable on the GEOSFP model `regrid` (RFC pure-io-data-loaders §4.1/§5.2).",
        "crs_provenance": "Former DataLoaderSpatial.crs '+proj=longlat +datum=WGS84 +no_defs' is now the structured GDD grid.crs {projection: longlat, datum: WGS84}.",
        "merged_from": "components/earthsci_data/geosfp_a3mstc_loader.esm",
        "merge_note": "Merged from the standalone pure-I/O file components/earthsci_data/geosfp_a3mstc_loader.esm, which is deleted by the same commit. The 0.x `X.esm` + `X_loader.esm` split existed only because a loader was a COMPONENT and a {\"ref\"} target had to contain exactly one component. At esm 1.0.0 a data source is NOT a component, not a coupling endpoint and not a scoped-name path root, and `data_sources` no longer counts toward a file's top-level system count — so one file may hold a model AND the data_sources that model consumes and still be mountable by {\"ref\"}. This registry entry is byte-identical to the one the deleted file declared (it was already mirrored here so this document would validate), and the deleted file's own top-level metadata — name, description, tags, created, authors, references — is preserved verbatim in `merged_file_metadata` so no provenance, citation or migration note is lost.",
        "merged_file_metadata": {
          "name": "GEOSFP_A3mstC_loader",
          "description": "Pure-I/O data loader for GEOS-FP (A3MSTC collection): 3-hourly time-averaged 3-D moist fields on layer centers on the native 0.3125°×0.25° global longitude/latitude grid, from the GEOS-Chem GEOS_FP 0.25x0.3125 archive.\n\nThis is one loader half of the geosfp loader+regridding-model split (RFC pure-io-data-loaders §4.1/§7; bead esm-3nc.2, following the esm-3nc.1 era5/wrf pattern). It is PURE I/O: it declares its source (url_template), the file variables it reads (with units), its temporal cadence, and its NATIVE grid expressed as a GDD Grid with a geographic (longlat/WGS84) crs descriptor. It performs NO reprojection and NO regridding — those are per-variable concerns of the regridding model (components/earthsci_data/geosfp.esm), which references this file as a subsystem via {\"ref\": \"./geosfp_a3mstc_loader.esm\"} under the subsystem key GEOSFP_A3mstC.\n\nThe removed co-located blocks: the old DataLoaderSpatial block (proj4 crs string / grid_type / staggering / resolution / extent) is replaced by the GDD `grid` (family + crs + dimensions + extents); the old per-loader `regridding` block (fill_value / extrapolation) is gone — regridding is declared per-variable on the model (geosfp.esm `regrid`). Because a `temporal` block is present, this loader seeds DISCRETE cadence (ess-v9a.5): the runtime refreshes the file buffers on its update schedule.\n\nMigrated from EarthSciData.jl@830435a065f27e99f10bba91107ca1730322cc6b:src/geosfp.jl (GEOSFPFileSet, filetype=A3MSTC). Split out of the pre-migration components/earthsci_data/geosfp.esm (esm-1c6s).",
