  "models": {
    "GEOSFP": {
      "reference": {
        "notes": "This is the regridding-model half of the pure-IO loader migration (RFC pure-io-data-loaders §6/§7; esm-3nc.1 era5/wrf pattern, bead esm-3nc.2). The pre-migration geosfp.esm carried both the GEOSFP coupler model AND seven co-located data_loaders blocks (six grid loaders GEOSFP_A1/A3cld/A3dyn/A3mstC/A3mstE/I3 plus a GEOSFP_hybrid_coefs kind:lookup table). The six grid loaders became, at 0.7.0, pure-I/O files referenced as subsystems under their ORIGINAL names (GEOSFP_A1 … GEOSFP_I3 → ./geosfp_<coll>_loader.esm). At esm 1.0.0 they are six `data_sources` entries in THIS file under those same names — a data source is not a component, so it neither needs nor may be a subsystem — and every observed expression GEOSFP_<coll>.<var> keeps resolving unchanged. The GEOSFP_hybrid_coefs lookup became the top-level function_tables geosfp_Ap_pa and geosfp_Bp (kind:lookup is no longer a valid DataLoader kind in esm 0.6.0).\n\nReprojection (RFC §6 step 2): every loader's grid.crs.projection is 'longlat' (geographic WGS84), so the reprojection rule selected by convention is ESD reprojection/longlat.esm (esd-47z.1) — the IDENTITY transform (a no-op for an unprojected grid).\n\nRegridding (RFC §6 step 3 / §5.2): declared per variable in the model `regrid` block. The A3dyn C-grid wind components U (x-edge), V (y-edge), OMEGA (z-edge interface) are staggered → B-spline interpolating regridder (ESD regridding/bspline_regrid.esm, esd-47z.3); every other consumed loader field (all A1/A3cld/A3mstC/A3mstE/I3 fields and A3dyn RH/DTRAIN) is cell-centered → conservative area-weighted overlap join (ESD regridding/conservative_regrid_overlap_join.esm). OMEGA's upstream zero-extrapolation (extrapolate_type=0.0) has no schema field and is documented in the A3dyn loader metadata.\n\nMeanWind coupling: the re-exposed top-level GEOSFP.U/V/OMEGA observeds preserve the couple2 contract (GEOSFP.U/V/OMEGA → MeanWind v_lon/v_lat/v_lev).\n\nsource_ref: EarthSciData.jl@830435a065f27e99f10bba91107ca1730322cc6b:src/geosfp.jl:410\n\nUpstream GEOSFP(domain, domaininfo; name=:GEOSFP, stream=true, spatial_interp=:linear) creates an MTK System with:\n  - @parameters: lon/lat (rad) and lev (1) from pvars(domaininfo); t_ref (s)\n  - For every varname in every GEOSFPFileSet collection (A1/A3cld/A3dyn/A3mstC/A3mstE/I3),\n    one DataSetInterpolator and one observed equation via create_interp_equation (uses interp_unsafe)\n  - Coordinate mapping: lon/lat in radians (loadmetadata converts from degrees); lev=1..72\n  - Staggering: geosfp_staggering() returns:\n      A3dyn/U   → (true, false, false)  # x-staggered (lon edges)\n      A3dyn/V   → (false, true, false)  # y-staggered (lat edges)\n      A3dyn/OMEGA → (false, false, true)  # z-staggered (lev interfaces)\n      all others → (false, false, false) # cell-centered\n  - Extrapolation: OMEGA uses zero extrapolation (extrapolate_type=0.0); all others use Flat() (clamp)\n  - Hybrid pressure: P ~ P_unit * Ap(lev) + Bp(lev) * I3₊PS\n    where Ap/Bp are DataInterpolations.LinearInterpolation tables indexed 1:73\n    (lev=1 → surface ≈ PS, lev=73 → 1 Pa). Encoded as the top-level function_tables geosfp_Ap_pa (Pa) and geosfp_Bp (dimensionless); P is observed = table_lookup(geosfp_Ap_pa, lev) + table_lookup(geosfp_Bp, lev) * GEOSFP_I3.PS.\n  - Virtual temperature: Tv ~ T * (1 + 0.61 * QV); Tv_sfc ~ T2M * (1 + 0.61 * QV2M)\n  - Layer-mean virtual temp: Tv̄ ~ 0.5 * (Tv + Tv_sfc)\n  - Coordinate metrics (lat/lon domain only): δxδlon ~ lon2m * cos(lat); δyδlat ~ lat2meters\n  - discrete_events: build_interp_event fires at each file collection boundary to reload buffers\n  - metadata: Dict(CoupleType => GEOSFPCoupler, SysDomainInfo => domaininfo)\n  - couple2 with MeanWindCoupler: maps GEOSFP.A3dyn₊U/V/OMEGA → MeanWind v_lon/v_lat/v_lev\n\ngt-p3ep resolution: the @register_symbolic interp_unsafe pattern for all file-variable equations is replaced by the data_loaders §8 mechanism (GEOSFP_A1.*, GEOSFP_A3*.*, GEOSFP_I3.* references). The Ap/Bp hybrid coordinate tables — formerly the GEOSFP_hybrid_coefs (kind: lookup) data loader, a kind removed in the 0.6.0 hard break — are now the top-level function_tables geosfp_Ap_pa and geosfp_Bp, resolving the fixed-table lookup gap for P.\n\ngt-6ohw gap (DataInterpolations.derivative): δPδlev and δZδlev require the symbolic derivative of Ap(lev) and Bp(lev) with respect to lev (via DataInterpolations.derivative), which is not yet representable in the ESM expression language. These variables are omitted. When gt-6ohw is resolved:\n  δPδlev (Pa): d(P)/d(lev) = d(Ap(lev))/d(lev) + d(Bp(lev))/d(lev) * PS\n    For the linear interpolation with unit spacing: d(Ap)/d(lev) at integer lev n = Ap[n+1]-Ap[n]\n    The upstream code uses: expand_derivatives(Differential(lev)(P_unit * Ap(lev) + Bp(lev) * PS))\n  δZδlev (m): d(Z_agl)/d(lev) — requires Pmid = P_unit*Ap(lev+0.5)+Bp(lev+0.5)*PS (gt-p3ep(lookup)\n    with lev+0.5 offset) and derivatives of Ap/Bp at lev+0.5 (gt-6ohw). Both gaps must be resolved.\n\nZ_agl gap (gt-p3ep(lookup)): Z_agl = (Rd * Tv̄ / g) * log(PS / Pmid) where\n  Pmid = P_unit * Ap(lev+0.5) + Bp(lev+0.5) * PS\n  Evaluating Ap and Bp at the fractional level lev+0.5 is an offset-indexed lookup (gt-p3ep(lookup))\n  not yet representable in the ESM expression language. Z_agl is omitted; when gt-p3ep(lookup) is\n  resolved, add:\n    Pmid = table_lookup(geosfp_Ap_pa, lev+0.5) + table_lookup(geosfp_Bp, lev+0.5) * GEOSFP_I3.PS\n    Z_agl = (287.05 * Tv̄ / 9.80665) * log(I3₊PS / Pmid)\n\nUpstream test values at (-155.7°, 39.1°) for domain '4x5' (EarthSciData.jl test/geosfp_test.jl):\n  P at lev=[1,2,3,71,72,73]: [102340.38, 101572.77, 100805.17, 2.0, 1.5, 1.0] Pa\n  OMEGA at lev=[0.5,1,1.5,2,35,70,72.5]: [0.0, -0.00385, -0.00770, -0.00652, 1.12e-5, 0.0, 0.0] Pa/s\n  Z_agl at various levels: 63.38 m (lev=1.5) to 80132.64 m (lev=72.5)\n\nDomain notes: the default domain '0.25x0.3125' is the native GEOS-FP global grid. Regional and coarser domains (e.g. '4x5', '0.25x0.3125_NA', '2x2.5') change the URL prefix GEOS_{domain}/GEOS_FP/ and the filename suffix. The transformed domain in the filename replaces dots with nothing and underscores with dots: '0.25x0.3125_NA' → '025x03125.NA'. This ESM documents the default 0.25x0.3125 global domain.\n\nChecked 2026-10-28 against EarthSciML/EarthSciData.jl PR #226 (head jialinl6:Oct_merge @87f8da1). δPδlev is now carried: upstream replaced the DataInterpolations tables with its own piecewise-linear Ap/Bp and their closed-form derivative (the slope of the segment below an integer lev), which an interp.linear over the 72 segment differences reproduces, so the gt-6ohw gap above no longer applies to it. δZδlev and Tv_bar (Tv̄) are gone upstream and removed here. Z_agl is still not carried: upstream now sums the hypsometric thickness of every layer from the surface up to lev, which needs T and QV at each of those layers (a column read the data-fed parameters here, one value per cell, do not give), and nothing in the SuperFast gas-only stack reads it. Inline tests pin PS and check P and δPδlev against upstream. Outside 1 <= lev <= 73 upstream's P extrapolates the end segments while interp.linear here clamps; GEOS-FP levels stay inside that range. EarthSciData #222 (interpolation on the true, non-uniform latitude knots of the half-polar GEOS-FP grid) and the PR's index-box subset reads are inside the Julia loader, which a data source here does not encode: an esm host regrids the source itself."
      },
      "tolerance": {
        "rel": 1e-06
      },
      "variables": {
        "lon": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "rad",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "Longitude of the model grid point (radians). Coupled to the simulation domain's longitude coordinate via param_to_var. Used for GEOSFP data spatial interpolation."
        },
        "lat": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "rad",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "Latitude of the model grid point (radians). Coupled to the simulation domain's latitude coordinate via param_to_var. Used for GEOSFP data spatial interpolation."
        },
        "lev": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 1.0,
          "description": "Hybrid vertical level index (dimensionless, 1-based). lev=1 is the bottom interface (P≈PS, near-surface); lev=73 is the top interface (P≈1 Pa). Layer centers are at lev=1.5, 2.5, ..., 72.5. Interpolation within the Ap/Bp tables is linear with unit spacing."
        },
        "t_ref": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "s",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "Reference epoch (seconds since the Julia DateTime epoch) from which the GEOS-FP file time axis is offset. Set from DomainInfo.get_tref(domaininfo) at construction time."
        },
        "t_interp_ref_I3": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "s",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "TIME INTERPOLATION (loader records_per_sample=2), I3 cadence. Simulation-clock time (s) of any cadence anchor of the I3 (instantaneous 3-hourly: T, QV, PS) collection — i.e. a time at which a fresh record lands, so the interpolation weight w_time_I3 is exactly 0 there. Together with dt_interp_I3 it locates the current time within its bracketing record pair WITHOUT the runtime injecting timestamps.\n\nGEOS-FP's collections are NOT co-phased, which is why this model carries THREE independent (ref, dt) pairs rather than era5_single.esm's single one: the native records sit at 00:00, 03:00, ... UTC The default assumes the run clock has t=0 at 00:00 UTC of the file's day; a runner whose t=0 is elsewhere must offset it."
        },
        "dt_interp_I3": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "s",
          "default": 10800.0,
          "description": "TIME INTERPOLATION: the I3 cadence step (s) between the two bracketing records — I3 is 3-hourly, so 10800. Must equal the EarthSciIO LoaderTemporal.frequency the provider brackets on, so this model's weight phase agrees with which two records the provider actually loaded."
        },
        "w_time_I3": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "TIME INTERPOLATION weight in [0,1) for the I3 cadence: the fractional position of the current simulation time t within its bracketing pair of I3 records, w = frac((t - t_interp_ref_I3)/dt_interp_I3). Because it reads the simulation clock `t` it is CONTINUOUS (per-step): w ramps 0->1 across each cadence interval and resets to 0 at the next record, so a consumer blending the two bracketing fields as (1 - w)*F0 + w*F1 varies smoothly between records instead of stepping.\n\nMirrors era5_single.esm's w_time; see t_interp_ref_I3 for why GEOS-FP needs three of these and ERA5 only one."
        },
        "t_interp_ref_A3": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "s",
          "default": 5400.0,
          "description": "TIME INTERPOLATION (loader records_per_sample=2), A3 cadence. Simulation-clock time (s) of any cadence anchor of the A3dyn/A3cld/A3mstC/A3mstE (3-hourly time-AVERAGED: U, V, OMEGA, RH, DTRAIN, ...) collection — i.e. a time at which a fresh record lands, so the interpolation weight w_time_A3 is exactly 0 there. Together with dt_interp_A3 it locates the current time within its bracketing record pair WITHOUT the runtime injecting timestamps.\n\nGEOS-FP's collections are NOT co-phased, which is why this model carries THREE independent (ref, dt) pairs rather than era5_single.esm's single one: the native records sit at 01:30, 04:30, ... UTC — the mid-points of the 3 h averaging windows The default assumes the run clock has t=0 at 00:00 UTC of the file's day; a runner whose t=0 is elsewhere must offset it."
        },
        "dt_interp_A3": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "s",
          "default": 10800.0,
          "description": "TIME INTERPOLATION: the A3 cadence step (s) between the two bracketing records — A3dyn/A3cld/A3mstC/A3mstE is 3-hourly, so 10800. Must equal the EarthSciIO LoaderTemporal.frequency the provider brackets on, so this model's weight phase agrees with which two records the provider actually loaded."
        },
        "w_time_A3": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "TIME INTERPOLATION weight in [0,1) for the A3 cadence: the fractional position of the current simulation time t within its bracketing pair of A3dyn/A3cld/A3mstC/A3mstE records, w = frac((t - t_interp_ref_A3)/dt_interp_A3). Because it reads the simulation clock `t` it is CONTINUOUS (per-step): w ramps 0->1 across each cadence interval and resets to 0 at the next record, so a consumer blending the two bracketing fields as (1 - w)*F0 + w*F1 varies smoothly between records instead of stepping.\n\nMirrors era5_single.esm's w_time; see t_interp_ref_A3 for why GEOS-FP needs three of these and ERA5 only one."
        },
        "t_interp_ref_A1": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "s",
          "default": 1800.0,
          "description": "TIME INTERPOLATION (loader records_per_sample=2), A1 cadence. Simulation-clock time (s) of any cadence anchor of the A1 (hourly time-AVERAGED: PBLH, T2M, U10M, SWGDN, ...) collection — i.e. a time at which a fresh record lands, so the interpolation weight w_time_A1 is exactly 0 there. Together with dt_interp_A1 it locates the current time within its bracketing record pair WITHOUT the runtime injecting timestamps.\n\nGEOS-FP's collections are NOT co-phased, which is why this model carries THREE independent (ref, dt) pairs rather than era5_single.esm's single one: the native records sit at 00:30, 01:30, ... UTC — the mid-points of the 1 h averaging windows The default assumes the run clock has t=0 at 00:00 UTC of the file's day; a runner whose t=0 is elsewhere must offset it."
        },
        "dt_interp_A1": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "s",
          "default": 3600.0,
          "description": "TIME INTERPOLATION: the A1 cadence step (s) between the two bracketing records — A1 is hourly, so 3600. Must equal the EarthSciIO LoaderTemporal.frequency the provider brackets on, so this model's weight phase agrees with which two records the provider actually loaded."
        },
        "w_time_A1": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "TIME INTERPOLATION weight in [0,1) for the A1 cadence: the fractional position of the current simulation time t within its bracketing pair of A1 records, w = frac((t - t_interp_ref_A1)/dt_interp_A1). Because it reads the simulation clock `t` it is CONTINUOUS (per-step): w ramps 0->1 across each cadence interval and resets to 0 at the next record, so a consumer blending the two bracketing fields as (1 - w)*F0 + w*F1 varies smoothly between records instead of stepping.\n\nMirrors era5_single.esm's w_time; see t_interp_ref_A1 for why GEOS-FP needs three of these and ERA5 only one."
        },
        "T": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "K",
          "shape": [],
          "description": "Air temperature (K). 3-hourly instantaneous 3D field on the GEOS-FP hybrid pressure levels. Sourced from GEOSFP_I3.T. Used in virtual temperature calculation Tv = T * (1 + 0.61*QV).",
